- Prevent results from one case from leaking into another case's XAI page.

### Model comparison

- Compare only models that actually ran on the same eligible evidence.
- Display model versions, available metrics, runtime, and failures honestly.
- Handle missing model results without inserting made-up values.
- Do not show a hard-coded “best model” or predetermined ranking.
- Make the basis of any recommendation explicit.

### Speaker verification

- Use real reference audio and an implemented speaker-verification model.
- Associate reference samples with the correct case, subject, uploader, consent/legal basis, and metadata.
- Do not treat a deterministic synthetic vector as a genuine speaker embedding.
- Do not generate a similarity score if the model did not compute it.
- Distinguish speaker identity similarity from deepfake detection. They are separate questions.
- If no real verification model is configured, display a clear unavailable state.
- Prevent unauthorized access to reference recordings and sensitive speaker data.

### Voice condition/disguise analysis

- Only display findings supported by an implemented and configured analysis method.
- Do not infer a person's health, intent, or identity from unsupported measurements.
- Label missing functionality and uncertainty accurately.
- Never fabricate results to populate a chart.

